# sizes: all
# A menu row that runs a command carries that command's chord under the
# ACTIVE profile at its right edge, muted (`app/render.zig`'s
# `menuChords`, read through `info_view_copy.chordOf`). The tree row's
# menu, in each profile: standard reads `Ctrl+N` on New file and
# `Ctrl+K p` on Copy path; vim binds neither, so those rows end bare,
# and both read `Delete` on Delete…. The menu's width comes from its
# rows, so the cells are the same at every screen size.
write notes.txt hello
open notes.txt
command tree.refresh
rightclick 4 2
expect screen contains "New file…           Ctrl+N │"
expect screen contains "Delete…             Delete │"
expect screen contains "Copy path         Ctrl+K p │"
expect screen contains "Refresh tree               │"
# The chord's first cell, in the muted grey (onedark's comment).
expect color 29 6 fg #80848d
key esc
command editor.use_vim
rightclick 4 2
expect screen contains "Delete…   Delete │"
expect screen contains "New file…        │"
expect screen lacks "Ctrl+N"
expect screen lacks "Ctrl+K p"
key esc
